WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:04.650
Hi this is Presh Talwalkar and today I am going to explain a math trick

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.690
of how you can multiply numbers just by
drawing lines.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:12.019
Let's say you want to multiply 12 by 13

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:15.410
For this one we will draw one line

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:18.910
and for the two we will leave a little bit of space

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:24.270
and we will draw two lines. 

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:30.120
For the other number, we will draw lines in the other direction.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.840
Now we will group together different lines and we will count the dots.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.940
Here we have six different dots.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.560
In the middle we have five different dots.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.560
And on the other side we have one dot.

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:54.319
And that's the answer 156.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.400
We will do another example.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.580
For 15 by 21,

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:05.030
we start out by drawing one line. 

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:09.830
Then we'll leave a little bit space and draw five lines.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.480
For the other number we draw lines in the other direction.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.660
We draw two lines here and one line here.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:23.360
We will again group the different lines

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.880
Here we have five dots.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:32.540
In the middle we have eleven dots.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:36.100
And the other end we have two dots.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.840
We will need to make one adjustment
because we have 11.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:44.490
We will need to carry this one over which will make 3.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.640
And our answer is 315.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.820
We can even do this for bigger numbers.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:02:02.700
For 123 we start out with one line and with some space two lines. And with some more space three lines.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:08.520
And we draw the other lines for the other number in the other direction.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.040
We again group the lines.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.540
We have three dots here,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.480
eight dots here,

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.100
fourteen,

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.660
eight,

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:26.020
 and three.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.239
Once again we're going to have to carry
this one over (from the 14).

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.660
So that's our answer.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:38.580
It'll be 39,483.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.680
You can even use this trick when a number includes 0.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:50.750
But one thing is when you draw this line
you should still draw the line, but 

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.970
put it in a different color or different
marking.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:01.640
And the trick will be that we don't count any of the dots for that line

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.420
So when we make the grouping, we have three dots here.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.080
For the second arrangement,

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.480
we're only going to count the dots for
the non-zero lines.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:18.680
So we have six dots here. We don't
count any of the intersections for the zero line.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:24.900
In the middle, we again ignore the zero line, which makes seven.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.849
Here we have two dots.

00:03:26.849 --> 00:03:28.969
And two dots here.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.960
So you can even use this method when you have a number that includes zero.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.980
The reason it works is you can even use it
for algebraic equations.

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:44.769
Let's say you have x plus 2y times x plus 3y.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.100
We will draw one line for the x,

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:52.150
and we will draw two lines for the 2y
and we will draw the lines in blue.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:58.030
We will put all the x lines in black and all the y lines in blue.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:02.470
The other number we draw the lines in the other direction

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.280
And again we make groupings.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:09.220
So here we have six dots and because

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:14.180
both of the lines are blue that means it's y-squared.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:18.180
In the middle we have five dots,

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:22.530
and these are the intersections of a black and blue line,

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.750
which means it will be an x and a y.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.840
On the end we just have one dot and
that's for two black lines so it's x-squared.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.920
So that's the answer.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:42.220
I hope you enjoyed this trick. Please subscribe to my channel. I make videos on math and game theory.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:46.620
